// Linear Sensors: a dark rounded square with the React logo that tilts in 3D as the phone
// tilts, its shadow moving against the tilt. RN: src/animations/linear-sensors (index.tsx,
// react-logo.tsx). Drawn in Rust: gpu/src/linear_sensors.rs, which reads the `gravity` sensor
// (useAnimatedSensor ROTATION's roll and GRAVITY's z, { interval: 20 }, both follow from it).
// A child may not send, so the root starts the feed while this demo is open:
// `send … = startSensorInput(surface="linear_sensors", sensor="gravity", frequency=50)`
// (@exact/motion, its `device.motion` grant); without it the square rests at the sensors'
// zero reading (rotateX π/8, rotateY 0), as Reanimated's sensor value starts.

component LinearSensors
  view
    canvas surface=linear_sensors() position="absolute" top=0 left=0 width="100%" height="100%"
      testId="linear-sensors-canvas" aria-label="Tilt the phone"
